--- body ---
## Context
Author decision (2026-11-09, option a): stop publishing per-project agent memory in this repo.
The harness repo is PUBLIC. `.gitignore` (lines 46-52) allowlists `projects/` and `projects/*/`,
so 1,085 files under `projects/<cwd-key>/memory/` are tracked: copies of the Claude Code native
memory stores of 44 projects, last touched 2026-10-27 (e483ae5c). They include 14 `user_*` notes
(e.g. chemin-de-voix `user_bio.md`) and 72 `infra_*`/`reference_*` notes; 7 files carry IP
addresses (tailnet 100.93.x.x among them). A credential-pattern scan found none. Found by the
chemin-de-voix memory-v8 raid (2026-11-09). rules/guards.md: memory stays in its project's
repository, uncleared material encrypted; these copies sit in another, public repo and were never
audience-judged as a batch. Projects that adopted memory v8 (JETP-observer, climate-finance-het,
padme, sen-causal-reading, fuzzy-corpus, chemin-de-voix; AEDIST in progress) now keep their own
`memory/`, so much of the export is superseded.

## Work
- Inventory consumers before removing anything: scripts naming `projects/` (seen:
  scripts/smelt_native_notes.py, scripts/probe-memory-symlink.py,
  scripts/census/repo-memory-reads.py, scripts/trace-stats.py, scripts/gaze_wall_time.py,
  scripts/enumerate-merges.py, scripts/local-ci-negative-controls.sh), the installer or any
  symlink that makes `~/.claude/projects/*/memory` point into this tree, and skills (smelt,
  roar capture) that read or write it. Decide per consumer: retarget, or retire.
- `git rm -r --cached projects/*/memory` (keep the local files where a runtime still reads
  them), drop the `!projects/` allowlist lines, and make sure nothing re-adds them.
- Anything the harness itself must keep from these notes: move it into `memory/` here after an
  audience review, private material only as `.age` via scripts/memory-capture.sh.
- Notes belonging to another project: that project's own memory deployment consolidates them
  (memory-v8 tickets), never this repo.
- Out of scope, separate author decision: scrubbing git history (filter-repo + force push), as
  with the cired purge.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] every consumer of `projects/*/memory` listed with its disposition; none breaks
- [ ] no file under `projects/` is tracked on main; `.gitignore` no longer allowlists it
- [ ] a test or check proves a new `projects/<key>/memory/x.md` stays untracked
- [ ] the history-scrub question is put to the author with its cost, not executed

## Imagine (raid 632b19, 2026-11-09)
No runtime reader of the tracked export exists: every literal `projects/` hit in scripts and
tests means `~/.claude/projects` (a real directory) or a tmp fixture; skills touch only the
native store. The 1,085 files (44 keys, last touched 2026-10-27) are a stale public copy.
Consumers that change: `scripts/check-personal-data.sh:6,10,31` (default scan targets drop
`projects/`), `scripts/resident_census.py:171-175` (builds `root/"projects"/*/memory/MEMORY.md`
from parts; its channel moves to the harness's own `memory/MEMORY.md`, else
`tests/test_resident_census.py` fails the gate: memory floor 1000 vs 0, `max([])`), `README.md:191`
(the tree listing). The 15 other grep hits are fixtures, docstrings or already `~/.claude/projects`.
Mechanics: `git rm -r --cached projects` (one pathspec; never `git rm -r projects`, the primary
holds ignored transcripts), delete `.gitignore:46-55` (the file is a `*` deny-all; those are the
only re-includes; no nested .gitignore), add an explicit `projects/` line. A pull deletes the
tracked copies from every clone's working tree: the ticket's "keep the local files" clause
holds only for ignored transcripts; the PR says so.
Audience: move nothing into `memory/`. Reason: each project's memory-v8 deployment owns its
notes; the harness's old key `-home-haduong--claude` (139 files) was NOT absorbed by v8
(`design/memory-v8/source-inventory.md:22,85` "path identity unverified", 66-70 "must not be
pooled"), it survives only in padme's local store and in git history. 1481 is told so (log line).
`memory/.provenance.json` lists project path keys: out of scope here, named in the PR.
Exit criterion 3: one `git check-ignore --no-index -q projects/k/memory/x.md` assertion in
`tests/test_attribution_capture_path.py` (already shells git); no new module, no CI probe.
Exit criterion 4: the history-scrub question goes to the author in the raid briefing (options:
no scrub / scrub user_* and infra_* paths / full scrub batched with the cired purge; ~2-4
author-hours plus freeze and re-clone on padme and doudou; default: no scrub, old, no credentials).
Blind-Spot pass: 4 material findings (census, README line, false "absorbed" claim, provenance), folded above.

## Plan
1. Red first: in the hunt worktree add the check-ignore assertion (fails on base, rc 1) and
   run `tests/test_resident_census.py` after a trial `git rm -r --cached projects` to see the
   gate failure for the targeted reason.
2. One commit: `git rm -r --cached projects`; `.gitignore` lines 46-55 → `projects/`;
   `scripts/check-personal-data.sh` defaults; `scripts/resident_census.py` memory channel →
   `memory/MEMORY.md` with test comments corrected; `README.md:191` removed; the assertion.
3. Evidence in the PR: `git ls-files projects | wc -l` 1085 → 0; `git check-ignore -v --no-index
   projects/-x/memory/new.md` rc 1 before, 0 after; `make check` (full: Python changed).
Dependencies: none. 1481 independent.

